(If you're using the React Compiler, much of this memoization happens automatically.)

## 2. Make filtering non-urgent with `useDeferredValue` (React 18+)

This is usually the biggest win. The input updates immediately, and the expensive list render happens at lower priority and can be interrupted:

```jsx
function Search({ items }) {
  const [query, setQuery] = useState('');
  const deferredQuery = useDeferredValue(query);

  const filtered = useMemo(
    () => items.filter(i =>
      i.name.toLowerCase().includes(deferredQuery.toLowerCase())
    ),
    [items, deferredQuery]
  );

  const isStale = query !== deferredQuery;

  return (
    <>
      <input value={query} onChange={e => setQuery(e.target.value)} />
      <div style={{ opacity: isStale ? 0.6 : 1 }}>
        <ItemList items={filtered} />   {/* must be React.memo'd */}
      </div>
    </>
  );
}
```

`useTransition` (wrapping `setFilter` in `startTransition`) does the same thing if you control the setter.

## 3. Virtualize the list

If the list has hundreds or thousands of items, render only what's visible. This often matters more than everything else combined.

```jsx
import { useVirtualizer } from '@tanstack/react-virtual';

function VirtualList({ items }) {
  const parentRef = useRef(null);
  const virtualizer = useVirtualizer({
    count: items.length,
    getScrollElement: () => parentRef.current,
    estimateSize: () => 40,
  });

  return (
    <div ref={parentRef} style={{ height: 500, overflow: 'auto' }}>
      <div style={{ height: virtualizer.getTotalSize(), position: 'relative' }}>
        {virtualizer.getVirtualItems().map(v => (
          <div
            key={v.key}
            style={{ position: 'absolute', top: 0, width: '100%',
                     transform: `translateY(${v.start}px)` }}
          >
            {items[v.index].name}
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  );
}
```

Alternatives include `react-window` and `react-virtuoso`.

## 4. Debounce, if filtering hits a server or is very expensive

```jsx
const [query, setQuery] = useState('');
const [debounced, setDebounced] = useState('');

useEffect(() => {
  const t = setTimeout(() => setDebounced(query), 250);
  return () => clearTimeout(t);
